<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Griffin Warrior Tomb</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1450 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century-bce">15th century BCE</a> · Also known as Grave of the Griffin Warrior</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Griffin Warrior Tomb is a shaft grave of the early Mycenaean period near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palace-of-nestor">Palace of Nestor</a> at Pylos, discovered in 2015 by Jack Davis and Sharon Stocker. Dating from about 1450 BCE, it held a warrior buried with more than 1,400 objects, including weapons, gold rings, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> plaque with a griffin and the finely carved Pylos Combat Agate, showing strong links with Minoan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>.</p></div>
